    "body": "# [Bugfix][collect-env] Report the cuDNN runtime version\n\n## Summary\n\nMake the `cuDNN version` field in `vllm collect-env` report the cuDNN runtime\nversion used by PyTorch.\n\n## Why\n\nThe previous implementation was named `get_cudnn_version`, but it searched\nOS-specific locations for cuDNN library files and returned their paths. It\ncould therefore report `Could not collect` when cuDNN was installed through an\nNVIDIA Python wheel, even though PyTorch could use cuDNN successfully.\n\nThis change uses `torch.backends.cudnn.version()`, which reports the runtime\nversion available to PyTorch. It also makes the field's value match its name:\nthe field reports a version rather than a library path.\n\nLibrary-path discovery is intentionally not retained under `cuDNN version`;\npaths and runtime versions are different diagnostics and should not be mixed.\nThe runtime lookup is limited to CUDA builds and falls back to\n`Could not collect` with a warning if PyTorch cannot initialize cuDNN.\n\n## Before / After\n\nIn an environment where cuDNN was installed by the NVIDIA Python wheel and\nwas usable by PyTorch, but was not registered with the system linker:\n\n```text\n# Before\ncuDNN version                : Could not collect\n\n# After\ncuDNN version                : 92000\n```\n\nThe test environment contained `nvidia-cudnn-cu13==9.20.0.48`; the reported\n`92000` is the version integer returned by PyTorch.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Installed the current worktree with precompiled artifacts using\n  `VLLM_USE_PRECOMPILED=1 uv pip install -e . --torch-backend=auto`.\n- Ran `vllm collect-env` and verified that it reports `cuDNN version: 92000`\n  instead of `Could not collect`.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Unit tests were not run; the change was manually validated through the CLI.\n- No model evaluation is needed; this changes diagnostics only.\n\nThis is a focused cuDNN runtime-reporting fix and is distinct from existing\n`collect-env` work such as #39817